# As check-of-a-dead-zone-is-asked-once-in-front-of-the-typed-copy.ir, with `table` in a scope of a function. A variable of a module is asked in front of its loop by Walker::buildLoopTwice(), whatever the turns run.
# A slot of a scope is not: each call of `outer` makes a scope with its slots empty. Here the walk goes by the value: no turn writes the slot, so its read stands in front of the typed copy, and so does the look at what was read.
# OPTIONS: check=Validate
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK: isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: = CheckInitialized {{*}}name="table"
# CHECK: = GetEnvironmentField
# CHECK-NEXT: = TypeTest {{*}}testedType=absent
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch
# CHECK: isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-NOT: = CheckInitialized
# CHECK-NOT: = ShapeTest
# CHECK: = Add {{*}}form=Integers
# CHECK-NOT: = CheckInitialized
# CHECK: Return
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell globalThis.unseen = x => x;
# ANSWERS: -991
